Core: shared buffers, textures and fences, exportable to another device, API or process.

NRI has no way to export a buffer's or texture's memory or a fence: BufferDesc, TextureDesc and
AllocateMemoryDesc carry no exportable flag, CreateFence takes no desc, and the Vulkan backend loads
one external-memory entry point for its own use only. A compositor or editor importing the viewport,
a second NRI device, or CUDA (cudaImportExternalMemory and cudaImportExternalSemaphore take exactly
these handles) needs it; imports already go through the wrapper descs.

This adds, in the shape the maintainer asked for on #49 (fields on the existing descs, no parallel
creation functions):
  - BufferDesc::shared, TextureDesc::shared: a committed resource in DEVICE memory with a dedicated,
    exportable allocation (VK: VkExternalMemoryBufferCreateInfo / VkExternalMemoryImageCreateInfo and
    VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo, allocated outside VMA so the export info can be chained; D3D12:
    D3D12_HEAP_FLAG_SHARED)
  - FenceDesc { initialValue, shared }, which CreateFence now takes (VK: VkExportSemaphoreCreateInfo,
    timeline or binary; D3D12: D3D12_FENCE_FLAG_SHARED, UNSUPPORTED for a binary semaphore)
  - SharedHandleType, SharedHandle and CoreInterface::GetBufferSharedHandle / GetTextureSharedHandle
    / GetFenceSharedHandle beside the native-object getters: a new caller-owned handle per call
    (VK: vkGetMemory* / vkGetSemaphore* Win32HandleKHR or FdKHR; D3D12: ID3D12Device::CreateSharedHandle)
  - DeviceDesc::features.sharedResources / sharedFences (VK: the platform's external memory /
    semaphore extension; D3D12: true)
  - EXTERNAL_QUEUE, a sentinel for TextureBarrierDesc::srcQueue / dstQueue naming
    VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_EXTERNAL, which the wrappers cannot express
The Vulkan backend enables VK_KHR_external_memory_win32/fd and VK_KHR_external_semaphore_win32/fd
when the device has them. Validation refuses "shared" outside CreateCommitted* and outside DEVICE
memory, a getter on an object that is not shared, and a shared object on a device without the
feature. NONE returns zero handles. D3D11, WGPU and Metal answer UNSUPPORTED. Applies on top of NRI
main 83fd010 and patch 0001.

